567	{\looseness=-1 \textbf{Cross-backbone generalization.}\label{sec:cross_backbone} RR-MoA is not specific to MOMENT. It wins all 21 MOMENT-small and MOMENT-large configurations ($27$--$81\%$; Table~\ref{tab:cross_backbone}) and 18/18 Moirai configurations ($3$--$31\%$), the latter showing that raw-signal routing helps even on LayerNorm-only backbones whose hidden states already retain routing information. On Moirai-MoE~\citep{liu2025moiraimoe}, which already contains sparse internal experts, RR-MoA still improves all 6 datasets by $37$--$90\%$ (Table~\ref{tab:moirai_moe}): adapter-level and backbone-internal routing operate on complementary axes. The two negative controls predicted by Observation~\ref{thm:mi_decomp}---Chronos and Timer-XL~\citep{liu2025timerxl}, neither of which uses instance normalization---show no collapse and no RR-MoA gain (4/18 wins, within chance; Appendix~\ref{app:cross_backbone}).}
568	
